to the start of your career,

00:01:11.068 --> 00:01:14.243
a man with a dream, training
in the gym day in and day out,

00:01:14.243 --> 00:01:18.172
if somebody said to you
you'll be as successful

00:01:18.172 --> 00:01:21.725
as you are now, what would
you have said back then?

00:01:21.725 --> 00:01:24.749
(clears throat)

00:01:24.749 --> 00:01:27.855
- I believe ya, that's
what I would've said

00:01:27.855 --> 00:01:31.413
because I did believe, I believed in it.

00:01:31.413 --> 00:01:33.611
I had very few people who told me that.

00:01:33.611 --> 00:01:37.930
I had a small, small,
small group of people

00:01:37.930 --> 00:01:40.502
that would tell me something like that.

00:01:40.502 --> 00:01:42.901
Other than that, it was
just me telling myself

00:01:42.901 --> 00:01:45.072
so if someone came up
to me and told me that

00:01:45.072 --> 00:01:48.240
all the way back then,
I'd say you're damn right.

00:01:48.240 --> 00:01:51.240
(soft upbeat music)

00:01:53.007 --> 00:01:55.701
I was thrown into a plumbing trade.

00:01:55.701 --> 00:01:57.470
Didn't give a shit about plumbing,

00:01:57.470 --> 00:01:59.414
didn't know anything about plumbing.

00:01:59.414 --> 00:02:01.627
I just went on that site because culture

00:02:01.627 --> 00:02:04.345
told me that that's what I have to do.

00:02:04.345 --> 00:02:06.270
I had done it for awhile
and then I realized

00:02:06.270 --> 00:02:08.617
this is not what I want to do.

00:02:08.617 --> 00:02:10.161
If this is not what I want to do,

00:02:10.161 --> 00:02:11.880
then what the fuck am I doing it for?

00:02:11.880 --> 00:02:15.206
And I walked out, 18 months in maybe.

00:02:15.206 --> 00:02:17.503
- There was a concern for
all of us, for his mother

00:02:17.503 --> 00:02:19.182
and for other, we didn't know what he

00:02:19.182 --> 00:02:23.099
was going to do, to be honest with you.

00:02:23.099 --> 00:02:25.324
- Earlier on, obviously I
didn't know what it was.

00:02:25.324 --> 00:02:27.055
I couldn't look to my mother and say,

00:02:27.055 --> 00:02:29.472
"Hey, this Irish man done it,

00:02:30.329 --> 00:02:31.670
I'm going to follow in this footsteps,"

00:02:31.670 --> 00:02:32.952
because there was no footsteps.

00:02:32.952 --> 00:02:36.477
I had to create my own
footsteps and follow them.

00:02:36.477 --> 00:02:40.500
They were a little unsure
at first but they support me

00:02:40.500 --> 00:02:41.986
and they know I would do it.

00:02:41.986 --> 00:02:43.539
If I said I would do
it, then I would do it.

00:02:43.539 --> 00:02:46.757
- Yeah, I don't just knock them
out, I pick the round John.

00:02:46.757 --> 00:02:48.578
Yeah, I said this, I'm
sure yous are probably

00:02:48.578 --> 00:02:51.962
all thinking this guy is
talking absolute dribble.

00:02:51.962 --> 00:02:54.426
He's not going to do what
he says he's going to do.

00:02:54.426 --> 00:02:56.481
Yous are probably all
sitting there thinking that

00:02:56.481 --> 00:02:58.402
but now here we are again, and I've done

00:02:58.402 --> 00:02:59.672
what I said I was going to do.

00:02:59.672 --> 00:03:01.142
I feed off this, I feed off this.

00:03:01.142 --> 00:03:04.126
I love this stuff, this
is what gives me energy.

00:03:04.126 --> 00:03:06.388
Saying I'm going to do
something, putting it out there

00:03:06.388 --> 00:03:10.987
for the world to see and
then going out and doing it.

00:03:10.987 --> 00:03:12.693
There's no better feeling
in the world than that

00:03:12.693 --> 00:03:14.004
and it's as easy as that.

00:03:14.004 --> 00:03:17.424
Say what you're going
to do and go and do it.

00:03:17.424 --> 00:03:19.112
When you're chasing your
dream and when you're

00:03:19.112 --> 00:03:21.770
working hard, chasing something you love,

00:03:21.770 --> 00:03:25.270
and completely dedicated, it just happens.

00:03:26.111 --> 00:03:28.946
You can't really notice it, you know,

00:03:28.946 --> 00:03:31.383
even still to this day.

00:03:31.383 --> 00:03:33.601
I'm in an amazing position
in my life but I'm

00:03:33.601 --> 00:03:37.420
still walking like I'm not, like I'm not.

00:03:37.420 --> 00:03:41.635
I'm still walking like
I'm not in this position.

00:03:41.635 --> 00:03:43.324
- [Interviewer] Absolutely.

00:03:43.324 --> 00:03:44.972
- I'm still walking like
none of this is even...

00:03:44.972 --> 00:03:45.873
You know what I mean?

00:03:45.873 --> 00:03:48.008
It's just something I
love to do and I just

00:03:48.008 --> 00:03:49.319
keep pushing and keep working hard.

00:03:49.319 --> 00:03:51.486
I can't pinpoint an exact moment for you

00:03:51.486 --> 00:03:56.049
but if anything, I always
felt like it was happening

00:03:56.049 --> 00:03:58.926
way back then and now it is happening,

00:03:58.926 --> 00:04:01.260
but now I almost feel
like it's not happening.

00:04:01.260 --> 00:04:02.093
Do you know what I mean?

00:04:02.093 --> 00:04:04.019
I want to push to something else.

00:04:04.019 --> 00:04:07.008
I'm always striving to push forward.

00:04:07.008 --> 00:04:09.695
Hard work pays, I put in
a hell of a lot of work

00:04:09.695 --> 00:04:11.693
all throughout this
build up and the fight.

00:04:11.693 --> 00:04:14.252
I pumped out more content than anybody,

00:04:14.252 --> 00:04:16.308
more content than Fox,
more content than ESPN,

00:04:16.308 --> 00:04:18.363
more content than BT Sport, more content

00:04:18.363 --> 00:04:20.990
than anybody on the mic,
more than my own channels.

00:04:20.990 --> 00:04:21.846
You know what I mean?

00:04:21.846 --> 00:04:24.056
I'm a mother fucking work
horse from all angles,

00:04:24.056 --> 00:04:25.741
not just in the gym.

00:04:25.741 --> 00:04:27.343
I'm building this media empire myself.

00:04:27.343 --> 00:04:29.509
We pumped out the content and
I'm very proud of how it went.

00:04:29.509 --> 00:04:33.484
The consistently daily
movies I was releasing

00:04:33.484 --> 00:04:35.820
from like a month ago, every single day,

00:04:35.820 --> 00:04:39.970
nobody's doing that so
I'm very proud of it.

00:04:39.970 --> 00:04:42.959
Work pays, hard work
pays, and we put in the

00:04:42.959 --> 00:04:45.926
fucking work and that's
why I'm sitting at the top.

00:04:45.926 --> 00:04:47.505
I put it all on the line, I show up,

00:04:47.505 --> 00:04:51.371
I perform, and I get
the results from that.

00:04:51.371 --> 00:04:53.374
- Weren't you working in
the plumbing business?

00:04:53.374 --> 00:04:56.327
- I was working in the
plumbing business at the time

00:04:56.327 --> 00:04:59.914
and I'm trying to think,
it would have been around

00:04:59.914 --> 00:05:04.038
that time that John ...
nah see, I had left the

00:05:04.038 --> 00:05:05.965
plumbing business, I had
left the plumbing business.

00:05:05.965 --> 00:05:06.864
- How bad was that?

00:05:06.864 --> 00:05:08.615
- The plumbing?
- Yeah.

00:05:08.615 --> 00:05:09.448
- Horrendous.

00:05:09.448 --> 00:05:11.195
- Were you actually in the trenches?

00:05:11.195 --> 00:05:14.638
- It was in an industrial so
it'd be like building this.

00:05:14.638 --> 00:05:17.039
It'd be like the plumbing
that would be needed

00:05:17.039 --> 00:05:19.129
in a place like this, six
o'clock in the morning

00:05:19.129 --> 00:05:21.619
and I used to have to
walk for about an hour

00:05:21.619 --> 00:05:23.299
to get to the motorway and then I'd stand

00:05:23.299 --> 00:05:25.474
on the edge of the motorway
and wait for a bloke

00:05:25.474 --> 00:05:27.674
to drive by so he'd give me a lift

00:05:27.674 --> 00:05:30.478
and the motorway was getting
a renovation at the time

00:05:30.478 --> 00:05:32.117
so it'd take me two hours,
two and a half hours,

00:05:32.117 --> 00:05:33.585
to get to the place that
was out in the country.

00:05:33.585 --> 00:05:35.257
Then I'd be there for ten hours working

00:05:35.257 --> 00:05:38.549
and I was a first-year so I
was the worst of the worst,

00:05:38.549 --> 00:05:40.040
you know, I was only a beginner.

00:05:40.040 --> 00:05:42.751
Then two hours to get
back in the traffic again

00:05:42.751 --> 00:05:44.185
which was a horrible, horrible time.

00:05:44.185 --> 00:05:45.281
I was like you know what?

00:05:45.281 --> 00:05:46.890
I don't want to do this
and then I just left

00:05:46.890 --> 00:05:48.951
and then I just stopped
going, didn't get out of bed

00:05:48.951 --> 00:05:51.169
and me dad was coming in
trying to beat me out of bed

00:05:51.169 --> 00:05:54.413
and we'd have fights and
usually, for a good while,

00:05:54.413 --> 00:05:56.271
I didn't really speak to me dad.

00:05:56.271 --> 00:05:57.848
We just kind of stayed
away from each other.

00:05:57.848 --> 00:05:59.568
Anytime I'd come across me dad, I'd ...

00:05:59.568 --> 00:06:02.515
Anytime we did speak was to fight.

00:06:02.515 --> 00:06:03.818
- You lived in his house?

00:06:03.818 --> 00:06:05.617
- Yeah, I was only 18.

00:06:05.617 --> 00:06:07.010
- But you didn't talk to him?

00:06:07.010 --> 00:06:07.899
Isn't that kind of awkward?

00:06:07.899 --> 00:06:09.761
- It wasn't, whatever, you know.

00:06:09.761 --> 00:06:11.921
- You just didn't have
a deep relationship?

00:06:11.921 --> 00:06:15.254
- No, but since this has happened, since

00:06:16.089 --> 00:06:17.608
the dream has happened, since the vision

00:06:17.608 --> 00:06:19.858
that I had has come true...

00:06:21.481 --> 00:06:23.483
And like he went through
tough times as well

00:06:23.483 --> 00:06:25.749
because he'd got testicular cancer

00:06:25.749 --> 00:06:28.553
and so he got sick and all in my head,

00:06:28.553 --> 00:06:31.325
I was thinking I done that
because he's worried about me,

00:06:31.325 --> 00:06:32.460
he doesn't know what I'm going to do,

00:06:32.460 --> 00:06:34.149
and all these fights that
were happening all the time.

00:06:34.149 --> 00:06:36.604
I'm talking full on fights,
he'd come in and punch me.

00:06:36.604 --> 00:06:39.034
- You'd punch him back?

00:06:39.034 --> 00:06:40.592
- Yeah, we were going at it.

00:06:40.592 --> 00:06:42.322
- Wow, what did your mom say about that

00:06:42.322 --> 00:06:43.683
whose so protective of you?

00:06:43.683 --> 00:06:47.564
- Yeah, I don't know, she
just stayed out of it.

00:06:47.564 --> 00:06:50.943
- Why did it get to that point
to where he was that mad?

00:06:50.943 --> 00:06:52.986
- Just because I was
doing absolutely nothing.

00:06:52.986 --> 00:06:54.164
I was out getting into trouble.

00:06:54.164 --> 00:06:55.422
- He was disappointed in you?

00:06:55.422 --> 00:06:57.547
- Yeah, basically, he
felt like I was a waster.

00:06:57.547 --> 00:07:00.863
I was a waster, got called that a lot.

00:07:00.863 --> 00:07:04.363
And then once I started getting that focus

00:07:07.423 --> 00:07:10.369
and realizing I'm going
to make this happen,

00:07:10.369 --> 00:07:14.145
and then now that it has
happened, I'm making it happen

00:07:14.145 --> 00:07:18.555
and I have a great
relationship with me dad.

00:07:18.555 --> 00:07:22.440
We talk all the time and
I even see energy in him

00:07:22.440 --> 00:07:23.635
and I see energy in me mom.

00:07:23.635 --> 00:07:27.497
It's pressing times for a
lot of people in Ireland,

00:07:27.497 --> 00:07:30.462
there's a lot of bad stuff
going on in the country.

00:07:30.462 --> 00:07:33.145
A lot of people are struggling,
everybody's struggling

00:07:33.145 --> 00:07:35.244
and since them seeing me chase this dream,

00:07:35.244 --> 00:07:38.146
it's giving them an energy
and I see a new lease

00:07:38.146 --> 00:07:41.614
on life in them and that
alone spurs me on even more.

00:07:41.614 --> 00:07:44.741
So it's all just a perfect
storm that is happening for me

00:07:44.741 --> 00:07:47.313
and that is why I have this tunnel vision

00:07:47.313 --> 00:07:49.160
and that is why I'm willing
to kill every single

00:07:49.160 --> 00:07:51.906
man in my path to get that belt,

00:07:51.906 --> 00:07:56.394
just to secure the future,
my family's future.

00:07:56.394 --> 00:07:58.320
That's what I'm doing it for.

00:07:58.320 --> 00:08:01.051
It's hard to say, but
when I was a kid I always

00:08:01.051 --> 00:08:05.218
visualized stadiums and even
when I was playing football,

00:08:06.072 --> 00:08:08.383
I'd kick the ball against
the wall and pretend

00:08:08.383 --> 00:08:10.089
that I'd scored a goal and I'd run off

00:08:10.089 --> 00:08:14.385
and I'd be raising my hand
and visualizing an arena

00:08:14.385 --> 00:08:17.369
full of fans and that was
something I'd done as a kid

00:08:17.369 --> 00:08:20.457
out on me own, just running
around kicking the ball.

00:08:20.457 --> 00:08:22.617
I'd always had these visions of something,

00:08:22.617 --> 00:08:25.035
but I just didn't know
what it was and then

00:08:25.035 --> 00:08:27.229
I suppose when I came to these events

00:08:27.229 --> 00:08:30.831
and I started training and
then I came to an event,

00:08:30.831 --> 00:08:34.656
I was like okay, this is it,
this is what I'm going to do

00:08:34.656 --> 00:08:36.914
and now I'm doing it.

00:08:36.914 --> 00:08:39.782
My experience is in cage wars
and all the other promotions,

00:08:39.782 --> 00:08:42.039
not just the promotions
before that as well.

00:08:42.039 --> 00:08:45.622
It helped prepare me
for certain situations

00:08:46.705 --> 00:08:49.857
that you find yourself
in but you're talking.

00:08:49.857 --> 00:08:53.064
Even fighting in the UFC and
then fighting on a McGregor

00:08:53.064 --> 00:08:56.897
show in the UFC is leaps
and bounds different.

00:08:59.575 --> 00:09:03.016
Everything has been a
learning experience for me

00:09:03.016 --> 00:09:05.414
and I take everything
as a learning experience

00:09:05.414 --> 00:09:07.243
and I look to grow from
it and you know what?

00:09:07.243 --> 00:09:09.171
That's why I keep growing.

00:09:09.171 --> 00:09:12.404
The Irish people might understand more.

00:09:12.404 --> 00:09:16.862
A young boy dreaming of
putting on the Irish jersey

00:09:16.862 --> 00:09:21.029
or dreaming of putting on his
favorite ball team's jersey

00:09:22.718 --> 00:09:24.981
and that crest, and lifting that club.

00:09:24.981 --> 00:09:28.217
This is my crest, these gloves right here,

00:09:28.217 --> 00:09:30.438
these UFC gloves, you know?

00:09:30.438 --> 00:09:34.605
To be the first man to put
these one, to lace these up.

00:09:35.821 --> 00:09:39.066
They're going to do the job and honestly,

00:09:39.066 --> 00:09:40.953
no one can take that away
from me, no matter what.

00:09:40.953 --> 00:09:45.138
Honestly, I don't mean to be disrespectful

00:09:45.138 --> 00:09:46.612
but I don't care about nothing else.

00:09:46.612 --> 00:09:47.878
I don't know about nothing else.

00:09:47.878 --> 00:09:50.036
I don't even waste my
time with something else.

00:09:50.036 --> 00:09:52.953
Just don't listen, I'm talking shit

00:09:54.078 --> 00:09:58.401
but if I talk about this, if
I talk about honor in combat,

00:09:58.401 --> 00:10:01.234
if I talk about the human anatomy,

00:10:02.175 --> 00:10:04.758
the way the human body moves...

00:10:07.231 --> 00:10:11.335
I've been listening to
laughter all my whole career.

00:10:11.335 --> 00:10:14.486
I've been listening to
them laugh my whole career.

00:10:14.486 --> 00:10:16.366
They've been laughing.

00:10:16.366 --> 00:10:18.932
What, an Irish man winning a cage war?

00:10:18.932 --> 00:10:22.868
Oh hell no, you serious, an Irish man?

00:10:22.868 --> 00:10:24.534
An Irish man win a fight in the UFC?

00:10:24.534 --> 00:10:27.018
Hell no, laugh, laughs all around.

00:10:27.018 --> 00:10:29.968
Okay, you got a win, now he
wants to win a world title.

00:10:29.968 --> 00:10:33.078
Hell no, he's all talk,
he's all hype, he's a joke.

00:10:33.078 --> 00:10:35.355
Laughter all around at the joker

00:10:35.355 --> 00:10:37.323
and then the joker goes
and wins the world title.

00:10:37.323 --> 00:10:38.676
Now he wants to win a second world title?

00:10:38.676 --> 00:10:40.046
More laughter.

00:10:40.046 --> 00:10:44.996
Listen, the sound of laughter
and the sound of doubt,

00:10:44.996 --> 00:10:48.913
motivates me so I'm
enjoying that, I seek that.

00:10:50.588 --> 00:10:54.233
I don't feel no doubt or I don't feel that

00:10:54.233 --> 00:10:58.005
going to fight any of these
other UFC bums right now.

00:10:58.005 --> 00:10:59.731
They need to rise up.

00:10:59.731 --> 00:11:01.698
Right now, they're down there.

00:11:01.698 --> 00:11:03.101
I've got this situation where people

00:11:03.101 --> 00:11:05.698
are truly doubting me like they doubted me

00:11:05.698 --> 00:11:08.637
at the very, very beginning
and that's motivating for me.

00:11:08.637 --> 00:11:10.382
That's what's going to drive me to the gym

00:11:10.382 --> 00:11:12.531
when I need to go to the
gym to put in that work

00:11:12.531 --> 00:11:15.021
to get that win so that's
where we're at right now.

00:11:15.021 --> 00:11:16.757
- Jose Aldo backed out.

00:11:16.757 --> 00:11:18.794
He was going to fight you, backed out,

00:11:18.794 --> 00:11:22.283
and said it was due to a rib injury

00:11:22.283 --> 00:11:24.947
but he's been cleared
to fight by a doctor.

00:11:24.947 --> 00:11:27.658
What do you think happened?

00:11:27.658 --> 00:11:29.629
- I mean the man is running scared.

00:11:29.629 --> 00:11:34.398
I cannot force a man who is not
willing to step in to fight.

00:11:34.398 --> 00:11:36.828
I cannot force him into
the octagon to face me

00:11:36.828 --> 00:11:39.611
but really, I cannot hold
any grudge towards him

00:11:39.611 --> 00:11:41.803
because I would not
want to face me either.

00:11:41.803 --> 00:11:44.553
(crowd applauds)

00:11:47.018 --> 00:11:49.624
I was going to destroy him.

